model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The runtime adapter replaces the single pool controller instance every few hours whatever the load, and cuts every request in flight at that instant; a replacement must not fail an agent's turn. The model gateway entry treats the platform's reset text or its retryable flag, never an overloaded one, as a controller reset, and resolves the controller again for each send because a stub that threw this error fails again at once. Before the first response byte, a safe read (GET or HEAD without an upgrade, excluding video status polls) or a model call is sent once more after one second. A model call's body is read from a tee beside the real send and held, up to 4 MiB, only until the controller answers; a larger body is sent once. Sending a model call twice costs only tokens, and the pool records each attempt on its own. A larger body, a second reset or a model socket gets the native retry advice: status 503 with an api error for messages and a server error for other model routes, with Retry-After of one second. It is never an overload answer, because the messages client gives up after three of those. A control write keeps its existing failure, because its callers may not assume it was not applied. A started stream is never replayed; a messages or responses event stream ends with the native retry terminal, an api error or a failed response, which the model clients retry by themselves, and a reader that leaves is not an interruption. A model call whose outcome is unknown after dispatch answers 502 with Retry-After of one second and never asks the client not to retry; tool calls keep their not-replayed answer. Every failed controller call writes one POOL_CONTROLLER_CALL_FAILED line with the attempt, elapsed time, closed message class and the platform's retryable, overloaded, remote and reset flags. Each event writes one POOL_CONTROLLER_INTERRUPTED line with count 1, outcome, saved, cause, method and endpoint template, and one pool_controller_interrupted observability adapter event joined by request identifier. Exception text, query strings and bodies never enter either."
    }
  }
}
